#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:5
#: 7d4c85ae344440d1a929395a1a8e4520
msgid "Electro Permanent Magnet Gripper (EPM688)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:7
#: 90736f8fe44240369c058d3b789794fb
msgid "This article shows how to use the `Electro Permanent Magnet Gripper (EPM688) <http://nicadrone.com/index.php?id_product=13&controller=product>`__ with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:11
#: 2e9e371a2e1e42fc8e8018cb5b91cf9c
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:13
#: 1677c6c1743b4bbeb621b3b2e69fc0a0
msgid "The *EPM688* (from NicaDrone.com) is a small (less than 4cm x 4cm x 2cm) Electro Permanent Magnet gripper capable of 7kg of force meaning it can hold about 1kg of cargo.  The gripping and releasing of the cargo if accomplished by delivering a short pulse to an electromagnet which reverses its field.  Objects that it grips onto should be metal or have the included `thin steel target square <http://nicadrone.com/index.php?id_product=15&controller=product>`__ attached to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:21
#: 45b0017c07ae4d9abd5a8bcf86782a71
msgid "The device accepts a standard PWM servo input and uses a 5V power supply.  Significant amounts of power are only required for less than 1 second when it first grips or releases the cargo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:25
#: 36299e6cfdb3453d833a0bea79ba7535
msgid "`See Kickstarter **Video** of the product here <https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/412473553/opengrab-open-hardware-electro-permanent-cargo-gri/widget/video.html>`__!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:28
#: e233f2179a434369807ba1bafe45b0a5
msgid "Connecting to a Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:33
#: 838b07b7f64a47f18a7d56c12b8a053e
msgid "The EPM is connected to the Pixhawk in the same way as a :ref:`servo <common-servo>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:36
#: 4808d3a34f9043559a2b9f1638e0d925
msgid "If using Copter, Connect the EPM to AUX OUT 1, 2, 3 or 4.  MAIN OUT 1 ~ 8 cannot be used because the EPM does not accept the 400hz update rate.  AUX OUT 5 an 6 cannot be used because they are reserved for :ref:`Relays <common-relay>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:40
#: 92e9a4a41faf4b0ea88f4e489d39e2f6
msgid "If using Plane or Rover where all pwm pins update at 50hz, any unused MAIN OUT or AUX OUT 1 ~ 4 may be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:42
#: 13a358d58abb46f3ac3e1d307d302d4d
msgid "A BEC or ESC should be used that can provide 600milliamps of current at 5V for the short period that the gripper is first activated to latch onto the cargo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:47
#: 84eacec6c67240e3bc0db600c3e6dbb1
msgid "Controlling from a transmitter using servo pass-through"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:49
#: 5c2e5c4137ac42169708001b2bf7026f
msgid "Unfortunately with the latest versions of Copter, Plane and Rover the EPM can be controlled either from the transmitter OR during missions. Either is possible but parameter changes are required meaning both methods are not available during a single flight.  Below are instructions for setting up manual control through a transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:58
#: c9e7aec25ba2434cae96098937232d1c
msgid "Control using the transmitter is accomplished by setting up \"RC Pass Through\" which means the \"input\" channel from the transmitter is passed through to the autopilot's \"output\" channel of the same number.  For Copter this means you must have a transmitter capable of 9 or more channels because the EPM is connected to output ch9 (or higher)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:64
#: 2b00fd1fb153454cb635ee0cc3342c3e
msgid "Assuming the above is possible for your set-up, connect with the mission planner.  Go to the Config/Tuning >> Full Parameters List and set the :ref:`SERVO9_FUNCTION<SERVO9_FUNCTION>` (or RC9_FUNCTION) to \"1\" (i.e. \"RCPassThru\").  Note that if the EPM is connected to AUX OUT 2 then :ref:`SERVO10_FUNCTION<SERVO10_FUNCTION>` should be set instead, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:69
#: 3391dbc9b00242ffba4f3c1d900e71bf
msgid "On the transmitter set CH9 to be controlled from a 3-position switch and the positions set as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:72
#: 220fbe7f17b94b7cbbea1a40093dd54b
msgid "*low position set to about **1100 pwm**.  This will release the cargo*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:74
#: f10f54dd982c46ecb338d4b307fa5191
msgid "*mid position set to about **1500 pwm**.  This is the neutral position, after pulling the switch high or low to grab or release, the switch should be returned to this position*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:77
#: 86b5e0413796456c8172ece51037a5b3
msgid "*high position set to about **1900 pwm**.  This will activate the EPM so it grips onto the cargo.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:80
#: aa9e675b5e7d446793fb33667c0812e3
msgid "To grab onto the cargo, bring the cargo close to the EPM and momentarily bring the switch high and then return the switch to neutral."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:83
#: 0b02cca086664c23ad9d9b97795a2c92
msgid "To release the cargo, momentarily bring the switch low and then return it to neutral."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:86
#: 1644beb6064742fc95c1eadecfe7f7d1
msgid "Note: the :ref:`Copter Ch7/Ch8 switch <copter:channel-7-and-8-options>` includes options for the EPM but these unfortunately do not function properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:90
#: 8af6c6a90c25449b8bdb362f1bf6fba5
msgid "Note: it is also possible (if using an older style, non ppm-sum receiver) to directly connect one signal wire from the receiver to the EPM's PWM pin thus bypassing the autopilot completely.  The image below shows the power line between the receiver and EPM connected but this is not correct and is quite dangerous because power spikes could pass through the receiver to the autopilot.  Only PWM and Ground should be connected.  The EPM should be powered from a BEC (not shown below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:104
#: 6d574504e99d46dc8a663719944a2c32
msgid "Controlling during missions and from GCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:106
#: 0a2b2cad3427460faa333db925e0f218
msgid "As mentioned above, the EPM can be controlled either through a transmitter or from the ground station (including during missions, aka \\ :ref:`AUTO mode <copter:auto-mode>`) but not both during the same flight. Below are instructions for setting up control through the ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:115
#: ca3a250a4b2841918b7d2377ea4b9ca2
msgid "Connect with the mission planner. Go to the Config/Tuning >> Full Parameters List and set the :ref:`SERVO9_FUNCTION<SERVO9_FUNCTION>` (or RC9_FUNCTION) to \"0\" (its default value). Note that if the EPM is connected to Pixhawk's AUX OUT 2 then :ref:`SERVO10_FUNCTION<SERVO10_FUNCTION>` (or RC10_FUNCTION) should be set instead, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:120
#: bfa6ca0bb5d94404a66a11f512987966
msgid "Create the mission you wish to fly and add pairs of ``DO_GRIPPER`` commands to grip or release the cargo .The EPM is returned to neutral after each command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:123
#: 554c296d458c4c968f9274bbcc7b6429
msgid "\"Ser No\" should be set according to which output the EPM is connected to (i.e. \"9\" = Pixhawk's AUX OUT 1, \"10\" = APM2's RC10)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:125
#: 4499ce682a7e4fb2b89874304603fd5f
msgid "\"PWM\" should be set to **1100ms** to release the cargo, **1500ms** to return to neutral, and \\ **1900ms** to grip the cargo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:131
#: 4de5c532206b40c29032e9a1c904eef7
msgid "In the example above the vehicle takes off to 20ft, flies west 548ft where it delays for 5 seconds, releases the cargo, delays another 5 seconds and then returns home."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:135
#: 3101e24ec2e74e18ab89384a5fd13137
msgid "In order to pick up the cargo before the mission begins, push the round black button on the EPM to momentarily turn it on.  A cumbersome alternative is to use the Mission Planner’s Flight Data screen's Servo tab to momentarily set the output to 1900 pwm (i.e. \"High\" in the image below) and then back to neutral (i.e. 1500 or \"Low\" in the image below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:145
#: 0d190856e99c46abacd54ae56e80f5e1
msgid "Specifications and more info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:151
#: 56204338c02c4e8f8393b5dc56152f98
msgid "The EPM has an onboard PIC12F MCU with an in circuit programming header to allow easy reflashing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:154
#: 45a0e11bcc2c402cb728a54ceaecb291
msgid "When first gripping or releasing the cargo it consumes 400mA for 0.4 seconds.  The majority of the energy is consumed to move the target into place and the rest realigns the magnets.  The on-board LED will blink rapidly 4 times when a switching cycle is being executed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:159
#: a5cd1fac182542758280baeb1dfb2e3c
msgid "On-board tactile push button: Allows toggle testing the EPM on/off having only the power connected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:162
#: f1b3550a7aa947e6b91e8a2cc573e01a
msgid "Full bridge Thyrisotor drive circuit increases efficiency and reduces capacitor size ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-electro-permanent-magnet-gripper.rst:165
#: ff09138323134d249b541707eedd47b5
msgid "Reduced magnetic interference allows mounting within 5cm of a compass (please test it with your application)"
msgstr ""

